##  Escape Hatch
Terraform provides [meta-arguments](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/resources/syntax#meta-arguments) to change resource behavior. For example, the `for_each` meta-argument creates multiple resource instances according to a map, or set of strings. The escape hatch allows you to use these meta-arguments to your CDKTF application and to override attributes that CDKTF cannot yet fully express.
The following example defines a provisioner for a resource using the `addOverride` method.
